  "name": "Partials morph (lydian breath)",
  "desc": "An additive sine drone whose spectrum keeps switching recipe. Two stacked voices share a C-lydian chord cycle but carry different partials: one the full harmonic series, the other odd-harmonics-only and hollow. Opposite <> masks trade them off cycle by cycle so the timbre morphs between rich and reedy while the chords progress, panned in opposite phase under a very slow filter bloom. Full/peak re-trigger (struct) so the bed breathes and, at peak, pumps.",
